From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:26:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: native host on egui-aros (one Intuition window, CPU or
 OpenGL interface)

VectorCraft for AROS runs vectorcraft-ui-egui's VectorcraftApp in egui-aros instead of eframe: one window through winit's AROS backend, the interface drawn by egui-aros's CPU renderer or by OpenGL (egui_glow over gl.library). Documents are rendered by vello_cpu as upstream.

GUI_RENDERER chooses the interface renderer: a Shell argument (--gui-renderer CPU|AUTO|GPU) wins over the icon's ToolType, which wins over CPU. CPU never opens OpenGL; AUTO falls back with the reason in the log; GPU fails visibly. The log records the requested and used renderer and, for OpenGL, vendor, renderer, version, GLSL and whether it is a software rasterizer.

Settings, libraries, recovery copies and the log live in VectorCraftData in the program's drawer (VECTORCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR, upstream's own mechanism). Upstream's settings modules are included unchanged by #[path]. Services: ASL requesters (paths converted between DOS and -nix names), clipboard text, OpenURL, atomic writes. Documents named in the Shell or passed by Workbench are resolved by DOS.
